# Clex vendor provenance

Upstream: https://github.com/Attempto/Clex
Fork base: 20960a5ce07776cb211a8cfb25dc8c81fcdf25e2
Import commit: ace2759c713c547fdd3a26f10095b2c370e69e77
License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Pristine: yes
First-party files: PROVENANCE, MANIFEST.sha256

The upstream tree (clex_lexicon.pl, LICENSE, README.md) is vendored
verbatim at the fork base pin. `Pristine: yes` binds the fork-notice
gate to content verification: every tracked non-first-party file must
match its MANIFEST.sha256 digest and carry no modification notice.
In-tree check: cd vendor/clex && sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256.
License is GPL-3.0-or-later per the clex_lexicon.pl in-file header;
upstream LICENSE (GPLv3 text) retained verbatim. Combination
conveyance record: root NOTICE.

Role: clex_lexicon.pl (97,541 lines, COMLEX-derived) is the
general-English base lexicon for the ACE front end. tools/goal.py
stages APE (copytree of vendor/ape) and copies
vendor/clex/clex_lexicon.pl over the staged demo
prolog/lexicon/clex_lexicon.pl; APE's prolog/lexicon/clex.pl loader
consults it per process. Ulex lookup precedence is unchanged;
goal.py check owns the ulex↔clex boundary (lexicon-redundant,
lexicon-shadow + audit/lexicon-shadow.tsv rulings).

A future modification ends pristine status: drop `Pristine: yes`,
follow vendor/ape's patch contract (prominent dated in-file notice per
GPL-3.0 §5(a)), bump the pin record, regenerate MANIFEST.sha256.
